Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:25:16 -0500
Subject: fix: a folder's rows stand as far apart as the list's

A folder laid its rows out with no gap at the open width, so a selected header
met the selected row under it, and two selected rows in a folder met too. The
rows of a list are 2 DIP apart (kTabVerticalPadding). The folder now uses the
same gap between its header and its rows, down nested folders and for the row
a collapsed folder keeps out. An open folder grows 2 DIP a row and the rows
after it move down by that. The drop bar's half gap already assumed the gap
(folders F39, F40), so it now sits in one. The rail keeps its gap by the
density (folders F43; sidebar Y12).

Why: the owner, 2026-11-05, from a capture (BACKLOG S-424).

Removable when: never as behaviour.
